# Everything here is either secret, large, or rebuilt inside the image anyway. The Dockerfile copies
# specific paths, so nothing below could reach the image — but the whole context is still sent to the
# daemon, and a secret should not travel that far.

# Local configuration. A .env on a developer's machine holds real API keys.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Version control and CI definitions.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Build output and caches; the image builds its own.
.gradle
**/.gradle
**/build
.kotlin
**/.kotlin
asset-tools/node_modules

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store
*.iml

# Documentation, which the image does not serve. The OpenAPI contract is under api/ and is copied.
*.md
LICENSE

# The release image archive Verify writes next to the build context.
release-image
